{"antibody": "<figure class=\"fig small\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 380 262\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"An antibody molecule, Y-shaped, made of four polypeptides. Two long heavy chains run down the stem and into the two arms; two shorter light chains lie alongside the arms. Disulfide bonds join the two heavy chains below the hinge region and join each light chain to a heavy chain. The tips of the arms are the variable regions, each with an antigen-binding site that has an antigen bound to it. The rest of the molecule is the constant region.\"><path class=\"f1 s-acc sw2\" d=\"M181 250L180.6 147.3L117.6 45.3L102.4 54.7L163.4 152.7L163 250Z\"/><path class=\"f1 s-acc sw2\" d=\"M217 250L216.6 152.7L277.6 54.7L262.4 45.3L199.4 147.3L199 250Z\"/><path class=\"f2 s-acc2 sw2\" d=\"M151.8 145.9L97.3 57.9L87.1 64.3L141.6 152.3Z\"/><path class=\"f2 s-acc2 sw2\" d=\"M238.4 152.3L293 64.3L282.8 57.9L228.2 145.9Z\"/><path class=\"fa s-acc2 sw2\" d=\"M145.5 90.3L117.6 45.3L102.4 54.7L130.3 99.7Z\"/><path class=\"fa s-acc2 sw2\" d=\"M125.2 102.9L97.3 57.9L87.1 64.3L115 109.3Z\"/><path class=\"fa s-acc2 sw2\" d=\"M249.7 99.7L277.6 54.7L262.4 45.3L234.5 90.3Z\"/><path class=\"fa s-acc2 sw2\" d=\"M265 109.3L293 64.3L282.8 57.9L254.8 102.9Z\"/><path class=\"ln thick\" d=\"M172 172L208 172\"/><path class=\"ln thick\" d=\"M172 188L208 188\"/><path class=\"ln thick\" d=\"M162 139.6L143.3 151.2\"/><path class=\"ln thick\" d=\"M218 139.6L236.7 151.2\"/><path class=\"fh s-mute sw2\" d=\"M96.1 29.55L105.1 38.55L96.1 47.55L87.1 38.55Z\"/><path class=\"fh s-mute sw2\" d=\"M283.95 29.55L292.95 38.55L283.95 47.55L274.95 38.55Z\"/><text class=\"tl\" x=\"4\" y=\"14\">antigen-binding</text><text class=\"tl\" x=\"4\" y=\"28\">site</text><path class=\"ln-m thin\" d=\"M38 32L96.5 68.1\"/><text class=\"tl\" x=\"4\" y=\"98\">variable</text><text class=\"tl\" x=\"4\" y=\"112\">region</text><path class=\"ln-m thin\" d=\"M62 102L109.5 89.1\"/><text class=\"tl\" x=\"4\" y=\"150\">light chain</text><path class=\"ln-m thin\" d=\"M84 147L135.6 131.1\"/><text class=\"tl\" x=\"4\" y=\"176\">disulfide bond</text><path class=\"ln-m thin\" d=\"M106 173L152.7 145.4\"/><text class=\"tl\" x=\"4\" y=\"222\">constant region</text><path class=\"ln-m thin\" d=\"M114 219L170 219\"/><text class=\"tl\" x=\"308\" y=\"40\">antigen</text><path class=\"ln-m thin\" d=\"M306 37L289.95 38.55\"/><text class=\"tl\" x=\"252\" y=\"154\">hinge region</text><path class=\"ln-m thin\" d=\"M250 151L211 152\"/><text class=\"tl\" x=\"252\" y=\"192\">disulfide bonds</text><path class=\"ln-m thin\" d=\"M250 189L204 188\"/><text class=\"tl\" x=\"252\" y=\"236\">heavy chain</text><path class=\"ln-m thin\" d=\"M250 233L211 233\"/></svg><figcaption>The structure of an antibody. The two antigen-binding sites at the tips are identical and complementary to one antigen. The hinge lets the arms swing apart. This is a simplified drawing.</figcaption></figure>", "hybridoma": "<figure class=\"fig small\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 338 466\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Flow chart of the hybridoma method. 1: a mouse is injected with the antigen. Spleen B cells that make antibody and myeloma cells that divide indefinitely are fused (2) to make hybridoma cells. 3: each hybridoma is screened for the wanted antibody. 4: the best hybridoma is cloned and grown in a fermenter. 5: the monoclonal antibody is collected and purified.\"><rect class=\"f1 s-acc sw2\" x=\"40\" y=\"6\" width=\"250\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\"/><text class=\"tl\" x=\"165\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1  Inject a mouse with</text><text class=\"tl\" x=\"165\" y=\"41\" text-anchor=\"middle\">the antigen</text><path class=\"ln\" d=\"M110 52L84 75\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><rect class=\"f2 s-acc2 sw2\" x=\"6\" y=\"78\" width=\"156\" height=\"74\" rx=\"6\"/><text class=\"tl\" x=\"84\" y=\"98\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Spleen B cells:</text><text class=\"tl\" x=\"84\" y=\"113\" text-anchor=\"middle\">each makes one</text><text class=\"tl\" x=\"84\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"middle\">antibody but does</text><text class=\"tl\" x=\"84\" y=\"143\" text-anchor=\"middle\">not divide for long</text><rect class=\"f2 s-acc2 sw2\" x=\"176\" y=\"78\" width=\"156\" height=\"74\" rx=\"6\"/><text class=\"tl\" x=\"254\" y=\"98\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Myeloma cells:</text><text class=\"tl\" x=\"254\" y=\"113\" text-anchor=\"middle\">tumour cells that</text><text class=\"tl\" x=\"254\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"middle\">divide indefinitely</text><text class=\"tl\" x=\"254\" y=\"143\" text-anchor=\"middle\">and make no antibody</text><path class=\"ln\" d=\"M84 154L120 177\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><path class=\"ln\" d=\"M254 154L210 177\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><rect class=\"f3 s-acc2 sw2\" x=\"40\" y=\"180\" width=\"250\" height=\"74\" rx=\"6\"/><text class=\"tl\" x=\"165\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2  Fuse the two kinds of cell:</text><text class=\"tl\" x=\"165\" y=\"215\" text-anchor=\"middle\">each hybridoma cell divides</text><text class=\"tl\" x=\"165\" y=\"230\" text-anchor=\"middle\">indefinitely and makes</text><text class=\"tl\" x=\"165\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"middle\">the antibody</text><path class=\"ln\" d=\"M165 256L165 275\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><rect class=\"f1 s-acc sw2\" x=\"40\" y=\"278\" width=\"250\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\"/><text class=\"tl\" x=\"165\" y=\"298\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3  Screen: test each hybridoma</text><text class=\"tl\" x=\"165\" y=\"313\" text-anchor=\"middle\">for the wanted antibody</text><path class=\"ln\" d=\"M165 324L165 343\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><rect class=\"f1 s-acc sw2\" x=\"40\" y=\"346\" width=\"250\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\"/><text class=\"tl\" x=\"165\" y=\"366\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4  Clone the best hybridoma and</text><text class=\"tl\" x=\"165\" y=\"381\" text-anchor=\"middle\">grow it in a fermenter</text><path class=\"ln\" d=\"M165 392L165 411\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><rect class=\"f2 s-acc2 sw2\" x=\"40\" y=\"414\" width=\"250\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\"/><text class=\"tl\" x=\"165\" y=\"434\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5  Collect and purify the</text><text class=\"tl\" x=\"165\" y=\"449\" text-anchor=\"middle\">monoclonal antibody</text></svg><figcaption>The hybridoma method. A hybridoma cell has the antibody-making ability of a B cell and the endless division of a myeloma cell. All the cells in the clone are identical, so they make one kind of antibody.</figcaption></figure>"}